# AI, Automation & Governance: My Learning Journey

## Introduction

Technology is evolving rapidly, and as a Project Manager working within the technology space, I believe continuous learning is essential to remaining relevant and effective.

This repository documents my ongoing learning journey in Artificial Intelligence (AI), AI Governance, AI Security, Workflow Automation and the practical application of emerging technologies to project and product management.

My goal is not just to understand these technologies theoretically, but to develop the practical knowledge required to identify opportunities, solve business problems, improve processes and contribute to the responsible delivery of technology solutions.

## Areas of Learning

### 1. AI Governance
Exploring the principles, frameworks and practices required to ensure AI systems are developed and deployed responsibly.

Topics include:
- AI Governance Fundamentals
- Governance by Design
- AI Risk Management
- Responsibility Allocation and Stakeholder Engagement
- Machine Learning Paradigms
- AI Security and Risk
- Generative AI Threats
- AI Security by Design and Red Teaming

### 2. AI Automation with n8n
Learning how to design and implement automated workflows that connect applications, process information and reduce repetitive manual tasks.

Topics include:
- Understanding Workflow Automation
- n8n Fundamentals
- Triggers, Nodes and Actions
- APIs, Webhooks and JSON
- Data Processing and Integrations
- AI-Powered Workflows
- Practical Business Automation

### 3. Practical Projects
Applying what I learn through hands-on projects, documenting the problem being solved, workflow design, implementation, testing and outcomes.

## Why This Matters to Me as a Project Manager

I believe the role of a Project Manager in technology goes beyond managing timelines, budgets, resources and deliverables.

It also requires understanding the technology behind the solutions we deliver, recognising opportunities for process improvement, anticipating risks and ensuring that solutions are useful, secure, responsible and sustainable.

Learning AI Governance helps me think about the risks and responsibilities associated with AI solutions, while workflow automation helps me understand how technology can improve operational efficiency and reduce manual workloads.

Bringing these disciplines together is helping me develop a broader perspective on technology delivery.

## Learning Philosophy

- Understand the concept before using the tool.
- Learn by building and experimenting.
- Document lessons, challenges and discoveries.
- Apply technical knowledge to real business problems.
- Consider security, governance and responsibility from the beginning.

## Progress & Projects

This repository will evolve as I learn, experiment and build. Practical exercises, workflow exports, project documentation and lessons learned will be added progressively.

**This is a work in progress, and the journey continues.**
